CC0 skinned human hand for `hand_backends/skinned_human.py` (epic #15150, #15148).

`hand_cc0.npz` is derived, by `build_hand_asset.py`, from three MakeHuman
files. All three are CC0 1.0 (public-domain dedication); see `LICENSE.CC0.txt`
and `SOURCE_LICENSE_STATEMENT.txt`.

Source repository: https://github.com/makehumancommunity/makehuman
Source commit: a8bc2d54ff0ac92e78ff71431b1023eda42bf482

| File | Role | Licence marker |
| --- | --- | --- |
| makehuman/data/3dobjs/base.obj | hm08 base mesh; the right hand and a forearm stub are cut out by skin weight | CC0 (MakeHuman asset licence) |
| makehuman/data/rigs/default.mhskel | "MakeHuman default skeleton", (c) 2020 Data Collection AB, Joel Palmius, Jonas Hauquier; bones, joints and hierarchy of the right hand | `"license": "CC0"` in the file |
| makehuman/data/rigs/default_weights.mhw | "MakeHuman weights", (c) 2021 Data Collection AB, Joel Palmius, Jonas Hauquier; skin weights of the right-hand bones | `"license": "CC0"` in the file |

Changes made: unit conversion to metres, a change of frame (wrist origin; x
radial, y distal, z palmar), quads split into triangles, the forearm opening
closed with a fan, at most four bone influences kept per vertex, and bones
renamed (`finger2-1.R` -> `index_prox`, and so on; the table is `BONE_MAP` in
`build_hand_asset.py`). The skin weights across the web between thumb and
index are smoothed (`thumb_web_smoothing` in `build_settings.json`) because
the original weights fold that skin over itself when the thumb closes; set
its iterations to zero to rebuild with MakeHuman's weights untouched. Vertex
positions, joint positions and all other weights are MakeHuman's.

MANO and SMPL-X are research-only alternatives; their licences are
non-commercial and those assets are not vendored in this repository.

The cut end of the forearm stub is closed with a dome generated by
`build_hand_asset.py` (`build_settings.json` `forearm_cap`); the dome is not
MakeHuman geometry. Zero rings gives a flat fan.
